# Fixtures are byte-stable synthetic substrate. Force LF everywhere.
#
# WHY: the repo runs core.autocrlf=true, so without this a fresh clone gets CRLF
# on disk while _generate_fixtures.py writes LF. Regenerating would then produce
# a spurious whole-tree diff on every machine except the one that last generated
# — which would quietly destroy the determinism the quarterly shape-refresh
# depends on.
#
# It is also the correct shape: real events.jsonl is written by
# atomic_write_text() with newline="" (no translation), so production substrate
# is LF on every platform. A CRLF fixture would not mirror it.
#
# Line endings on Windows are called out as a known scar in DEVELOPMENT.md.
* text eol=lf
